msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:20 9606ecfeaf374bb8963efb126052d859
msgid ""
"Python 3.10 reached end of life on 2026-10-01. `findfmt` 1.1 requires "
"Python 3.11 or newer and is tested on Python 3.11 through 3.15 on Linux, "
"macOS, and Windows (#441)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:23 99ac14670dd2466b846994d1fd063fdb
msgid ""
"On Python 3.10, installers keep selecting the latest compatible 1.0.x "
"release, because 1.1 declares `requires-python = \">=3.11\"`. To make "
"that explicit, pin the 1.0 series:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:31 9a94b9a48fda4b2a8e5279d6ef7bb0b1
msgid ""
"Only the latest release receives fixes (see the [security "
"policy](https://github.com/bdperkin/findfmt/blob/main/SECURITY.md)), so "
"upgrade Python when you can. See the [compatibility "
"guide](../quality/compatibility.md) for the full support policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:36 5757b72d33924578b241939f6056f059
msgid "3. Human-Readable Sizes Use IEC Binary Units"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:38 3ad9860c688a4f57a553ac307f210cd8
msgid ""
"Sizes are calculated in powers of 1024, and the labels now say so (#352)."
" The numbers are unchanged; only the unit labels differ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:41 f6801ae8d3a8441597c5f0ddb7a334a4
msgid ""
"On the command line, `-h` / `--human-readable` output changes from "
"single-letter units to IEC labels:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:54 1e5a7512f964410a874d6e55b4e869ef
msgid ""
"In the Python API, `findfmt.sizes.format_size()` changes from `KB`/`MB` "
"to `KiB`/`MiB`, matching `format_size_binary()`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:63 8de9485cd7874b4f881793560fd9bc1b
msgid ""
"If you parse sizes with a regular expression, accept the new labels, for "
"example `(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?) ?([KMGTP]i?B?|B)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:66 e7f76c46a3404bbfaa7c3fff666cb83f
msgid "4. `SortKey` and `OutputFormat` Render as Their Value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:68 fa9e6eab46994498bd85cc40150ef6d2
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`findfmt.SortKey` and `findfmt.OutputFormat` are now `enum.StrEnum` "
"subclasses (#441). As a result, `str()`, `format()`, f-strings, and `%s` "
"formatting return the member's value instead of the class-qualified name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:79 ef6b909ed7624bedac27f485c412fa59
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Comparisons with strings, hashing, `repr()`, JSON output, CLI help, and "
"configuration handling are unchanged, so `SortKey.SIZE == \"size\"` is "
"still true. If you relied on the old text, build it explicitly: "
"`f\"{type(member).__name__}.{member.name}\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:83 135589f336994158bc2456f8f3d8b301
msgid "5. Wrapper Commands Exit Non-Zero on Errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:85 22cd3b9ef97841d38a7df2a457aba131
msgid ""
"The wrapper commands (`findfiles`, `findfilefmt`, `findfilemime`, "
"`findfmt0`, `findshebang`, and `findsummary`) now exit with status 1 when"
" they stop with an error that carries a message instead of a numeric "
"status (#373). Previously they exited with status 0 in that case, hiding "
"the failure. The `findfmt` command itself is not affected, and normal "
"runs still exit with status 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:90 c63328ca76ab4ee7bd0340b2a2f7cc75
msgid ""
"If a script ran a wrapper command and ignored its exit status, treat a "
"non-zero status as a failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:92 e3c1f0bcdd3f4c95a9d8511eec703409
msgid "6. New: `--exit-status` for Scripts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:94 2a6af9e4b447496baea04fa8b1462c0c
msgid ""
"`findfmt` still exits with status 0 when nothing matches. Pass the new "
"`--exit-status` option to get `grep`-style behavior, where no matches "
"means exit status 1 (#367):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:103 8b4e48604fa54060a3f64bab80e0ef84
msgid "7. Platform Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/upgrading.md:105 35c4b43edaea488b96c1589a5c28eb40
msgid ""
"Python 3.15 is now fully supported and required to pass CI on Linux, "
"macOS, and Windows, and the container image (`ghcr.io/bdperkin/findfmt`) "
"runs on Python 3.14 (#335, #440). No action is needed. For everything "
"else in this release, see the "
"[changelog](https://github.com/bdperkin/findfmt/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)."
msgstr ""
